---
source: crates/standalone/fixture/src/lib.rs
---
Take a site down.

Usage: ink abuse suspend [OPTIONS] <SITE>

Examples
  # Take the site down, naming the report that led to it
  ink abuse suspend 0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef --kind phishing --report fedcba9876543210fedcba9876543210

Arguments
  <SITE>  The site's id, as `ink abuse list` or the site's owner gives it

Options
      --kind <KIND>  Why: phishing, malware, illegal, impersonation, spam or
                     other [default: other]
      --report <ID>  The report that led to it, as `ink abuse list` shows its id

Account
      --api <URL>          The API's address, `http://host[:port]`;
                           `account.api` in the config file [env: INK_API]
      --timeout <SECONDS>  Seconds one call may take [default: 30]
                           [env: INK_TIMEOUT]

Notes
  A suspended site serves a notice and takes no deploy, build or change; its
  files stay and come back whole when the suspension is lifted. Only the
  operator's key may do this: it is the key `ink login --data` made.

Exit codes
  0  Done
  2  Wrong usage: no API named, a key that is none, a private key that would
     print to a terminal
  3  No key, or the API refused the signature, or nobody approved the key in
     time
  4  The API could not be reached or failed; safe to retry

Environment
  INK_API       The address of the API, as --api
  INK_SITE      The site's id, as --site
  INK_KEY       The private key to sign requests with, for a CI job; never a
                flag, so it stays out of process lists. `ink login` keeps one in
                the config folder instead
  INK_KEY_FILE  A file that holds that key, in place of INK_KEY

Docs    https://github.com/uses-ink/uses.ink/blob/main/docs/cli.md
Global  -C, --json, -q, -v, --color, --no-progress, --log, --log-file
        (see `ink --help`)
